Theorem RL-19: ThreadReachability derives from Locality and the call graph

  Preconditions:
    - Locality is the converged escape dimension.
    - The call graph supplies a thread-boundary reachability signal.

  Soundness property:
    Forall value v:

      (P1) known Locality with no crossing yields ThreadReachability.confined.

      (P2) a proven crossing yields potentiallyShared.

      (P3) Unknown Locality yields potentiallyShared even without a crossing.

    The fact constrains physical safety capability without selecting an opcode,
    synchronization primitive, or memory ordering.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive Locality x call-graph enumeration with Unknown fail-closed.

    Part (P1/P2/P3) - reachability grid:
      function local + no crossing -> confined
      escaping + no crossing -> confined
      escaping + crossing -> potentiallyShared
      unknown + no crossing -> potentiallyShared
      Coverage gate: 4 reachability cases.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY - section_08::verify_rl19_thread_reachability;
        threadReachabilityFrom derivation)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)
      refinement (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-19 by deriving ThreadReachability from Locality and call-graph boundary evidence with Unknown mapped to potentiallyShared
